        "full": "You hold a mixed view of what truth is. Some knowledge strikes you as plain fact about the world, and other knowledge as a human construction that happens to work, and your answers suggest you treat the difference as real rather than embarrassing. The middle of this axis is less a fence-sit than a map with different territories on it: physics one way, money and manners another, with a contested border between. This usually reflects the view that \"is it real or constructed\" is a question you ask per domain, not once for everything. It tends to make you fluent in both registers, able to talk mechanism with realists and genealogy with constructivists. The strength of this position is its accuracy to how inquiry actually behaves across fields; the cost is the border patrol, since the hard cases, mathematics, morality, mind, sit exactly on the line and your map has to rule on them one by one. Your moral_ground axis is one of those border rulings made explicit. A middle score here is a worked-out division of territory.",
