    "centralQuestion": "Are some things right or wrong independently of what anyone believes, or are values something humans feel, make, or agree on?",
    "shortDefinition": "Whether morality is discovered or made: real facts about right and wrong, or human constructions given a human account.",
    "expandedDefinition": "This axis asks what moral claims are. The realist pole holds that some things are right or wrong the way facts are facts, independent of belief, so moral disagreement has high stakes because someone can actually be mistaken. The anti-realist pole holds that a complete description of the world would not include wrongness among its ingredients: values are felt, made, or agreed, and the honest account of them is human rather than metaphysical. The axis does not measure moral seriousness; anti-realists can hold fierce commitments, and realists can hold theirs with humility. It measures the story you tell about what those commitments are.",
