    "expandedDefinition": "This is the metaphysics of meaning, deliberately separate from the practice axis. The realist pole holds that some things matter in themselves: purpose is found, not invented, resting on God, objective value, or an order meaning can stand on, so significance is something you can be right or wrong about. The constructivist pole holds that the universe is silent about what matters, so the authorship falls to us: mattering is something people do, and commitment is a deliberate act rather than a discovery. The middle receives meaning in some rooms of life and builds it in others. Neither pole has a monopoly on living meaningfully; they disagree about what a meaningful life is answering to.",
