        "full": "For you, justice faces fully forward: the point is to repair harm, change what produced it, and prevent the next one, not to balance a ledger. This usually assumes that behaviour has causes and that causes can be treated, so a response that adds suffering without subtracting harm is simply more harm, whatever it expresses. It tends to make you ask what a sentence accomplishes rather than what it says, and to read the retributive intuitions, strong in you as in everyone, as feelings to understand rather than verdicts to institutionalize. In practice you likely measure systems by re-offense, reintegration, and victims made whole. The strength of this position is that it points every resource at the future, the only place harm can still be prevented; its blind spot is expression's real work, since naming wrongs, vindicating victims, and marking limits do social labor that pure prevention leaves undone, and communities notice the vacancy. Your freewill_practice and determinism axes show the frame this consistency runs on. This is not softness on harm; it takes harm seriously enough to demand that the response actually reduce it.",
        "short": "Suffering added without harm subtracted is just more harm: point everything at prevention and repair. The strength is resources aimed where harm can still change; the blind spot is the social work of naming and marking left undone."
